hadiths[229]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10472","Maslamah ibn Mukhallad (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Whoever conceals a Muslim in this world, Allah will conceal him in this world and the Hereafter. Whoever delivers one in distress, Allah will relieve for him a distress among the distresses of the Day of Resurrection. Whoever occupies himself with the need of his brother, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will be occupied with his need.""**"
"10473","Artah ibn al-Mundhir al-Sakuni (may Allah be pleased with him) was visited by a man who said, ""I have a neighbor who drinks wine and commits shameful deeds; shall I report his affair to the ruler?"" Artah replied, ""I killed ninety-nine polytheists before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it would not please me to have killed the like of them over again if in exchange I were to tear away the covering of a Muslim."" He said: > **""It would not please me to kill the like of them and to tear away the covering of a Muslim.""**"
"10474","Laqit ibn Artah al-Sakuni (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked by a man, ""We have a neighbor who drinks wine and commits shameful deeds; shall I raise his case to the ruler?"" He answered, ""I killed ninety-nine alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I would not love to have killed the like of them and to have torn away the covering of a Muslim."" He said: > **""I would not love to have killed the like of them and to have torn away the covering of a Muslim.""**"
"10475","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and addressed the people so loudly that even the sheltered maidens in their chambers heard him. He said: > **""O people, O company of those who believe with their tongues while faith has not reached their hearts: do not harm the Muslims and do not pursue their hidden faults. For whoever pursues the hidden fault of his brother, Allah will pursue his hidden fault until He exposes him for it even in the belly of his house.""**"
"10476","Abu Said al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""No believer sees a private fault of his brother and conceals it for him except that Allah will admit him to Paradise.""** In another wording: > **""Except that Allah will admit him to Paradise on account of it.""**"
"10477","Nubayt ibn Sharit (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Whoever conceals the sanctity of a believing woman, Allah will shield him from the Fire.""**"
"10478","Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: > **""Whoever conceals a private fault, it is as though he gave life to a buried infant girl from her grave.""**"
"10479","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Whoever sees a breach in his brother's religion and conceals him concerning it, it will be a good deed for him on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"10480","Shihab, a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: > **""Whoever conceals a matter for a believer, it is as though he gave life to a dead person.""**"
"10481","Masruq said: Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) came out to the people at the house and said to them, ""Whoever among you has come seeking a ruling, let him sit in his place. Whoever among you has come as a disputant, let him honor his opponent until I judge between them. And whoever among you has come to inform us of a private fault which Allah has covered, let him cover himself with the covering of Allah and consign it to the One who owns its forgiveness, for I do not own its forgiveness. I can only establish the fixed penalty upon him."" He said: > **""Let him cover himself with the covering of Allah, and let him consign it to the One who owns its forgiveness, for I do not own its forgiveness.""**"
"10482","Ibrahim (al-Nakhai) said: A man came to Abd Allah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) wearing embalming perfume, and when Ibn Masud saw him and smelled the perfume upon him he said, ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of this."" The man then came forward and mentioned that he had lain with his wife's slave-girl, and asked Ibn Masud to establish the penalty upon him. Ibn Masud replied: > **""Seek Allah's forgiveness, repent to Him, conceal it for yourself, and if you are able to free her, then do so.""**"
"10483","Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""When you see your brother commit a sin, do not become helpers of Satan against him, saying, 'O Allah, disgrace him; O Allah, curse him.' Rather ask Allah for well-being. For we, the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would say nothing about any man until we knew upon what he died. If his end was sealed with good, we knew he had attained good; and if his end was sealed with evil, we feared for him on account of his deeds."" He said: > **""Do not become helpers of Satan against him. Rather ask Allah for well-being.""**"
"10484","In another wording from him: Rather supplicate for him. He said: > **""Rather supplicate to Allah that He turn to him in repentance and have mercy upon him.""**"
"10485","Abu al-Tufayl (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, meaning Maiz ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): > **""Do not revile him.""**"
"10486","Al-Saib ibn Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A man was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said, ""O Messenger of Allah, this man has stolen the saddle-blanket of a camel"" — or, the narrator doubted, ""the blanket of an animal."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""I do not think he did it.""** They then said, ""O Messenger of Allah, this man has stolen."" He said: > **""I do not think he did it.""** This continued until the man bore witness against himself repeatedly. The Prophet then said: > **""Take him away and cut off his hand, then bring him to me.""** They took him, cut off his hand, and brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: > **""Woe to you, repent to Allah.""** The man said, ""I repent to Allah."" The Prophet said: > **""O Allah, turn to him in repentance.""**"
"10487","Al-Shabi said: Shuraha al-Hamdaniyyah came to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, ""I have committed adultery."" Ali said to her, ""Perhaps you spoke out of jealousy? Perhaps you saw it in your dream? Perhaps you were coerced?"" To each of these she answered, ""No."" He asked: > **""Perhaps you were jealous? Perhaps you saw it in your dream? Perhaps you were coerced?""**"
"10488","In one wording Ali asked: > **""Perhaps your husband came to you?""**"
"10489","Al-Qasim said: Abd Allah — meaning Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) — said: > **""Ward off the fixed penalty and execution from the servants of Allah as far as you are able.""**"
"10490","Yala ibn Murrah (may Allah be pleased with him) was with Ziyad when a man came and testified, then altered his testimony. Ziyad said, ""I will surely cut off your tongue."" Yala said to him, ""Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that Allah said:"" > **""Do not mutilate My servants.""** Ziyad then let the man go. In one wording with al-Tabarani, the Prophet said: > **""Do not mutilate the servants of Allah.""**"
"10491","Al-Mughirah ibn Shubah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: > **""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation.""** In al-Tabarani's wording, al-Mughirah, the grandson of al-Mughirah, said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shubah passed through al-Hirah and found people who had set up a fox as a target and were shooting at it. He stopped before them and said: > **""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding mutilation.""**"
"10492","Al-Hakam ibn Umayr and Aidh ibn Qurt (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Do not mutilate anything among Allah's creation in which there is a soul.""**"
"10493","Ismail ibn Rashid said, reporting the account of Ibn Muljim — may Allah curse him and his companions — concerning the death of Ali and his killing, that Ali said to al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both): > **""If I survive, I will decide my judgment concerning him. If I perish from this blow of his, then strike him one blow and do not mutilate him, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding mutilation, even of a rabid dog.""**"
"10494","Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) said: > **""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plunder and mutilation.""**"
"10495","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: > **""Whoever mutilates his brother, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all mankind.""**"
"10496","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported: > **""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation.""**"
"10497","Zayd ibn Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): > **""He forbade plunder and mutilation.""**"
"10498","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said: Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) came with some slave-girls of hers, her sight having gone, and asked, ""Where is al-Hajjaj?"" We said, ""He is not here."" She said, ""Order him to grant us these bones, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding mutilation."" She said: > **""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding mutilation.""**"
"10499","Imran ibn Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them, commanded them to give charity, and forbade them mutilation. He said: > **""He commanded us to give charity and forbade us mutilation.""**"
"10500","Abu Salih al-Hanafi reported from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — he thought it was Ibn Umar — who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: > **""Whoever mutilates one possessed of a soul and then does not repent, Allah will mutilate him on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"10501","Abd Allah — meaning Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) — said: > **""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that any among the children of Adam be castrated.""**"
"10502","Uqbah ibn Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of the hadith before it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): > **""Lifted from my community are mistake, forgetfulness, and what they are coerced into.""**"
"10503","Imran ibn Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: > **""Overlooked for my community is what their souls whisper to them, so long as they do not speak of it or act upon it.""**"
"10504","Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: > **""Indeed Allah has overlooked three things for my community: mistake, forgetfulness, and what they are compelled to do.""**"
"10505","Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: > **""Guarantee for me deliberate deeds, and I will guarantee for you mistaken ones.""**"
"10506","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it — the like of the hadith before it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): > **""Lifted from my community are mistake, forgetfulness, and what they are coerced into.""**"
"10507","Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""I do not fear mistakes for you, but I fear deliberate deeds for you.""**"
"10508","Uthman ibn Hayyan said: I used to visit Umm al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with her) and write in her presence. Once I took a louse — or a flea — and threw it into the fire. She said, ""O my son, do not do that, for I heard Abu al-Darda say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say:"" > **""None is punished with the punishment of Allah.""** In al-Bazzar's wording the Prophet said: > **""None punishes with the Fire except the Lord of the Fire.""**"
"10509","Bishr ibn Ubayd Allah — an aged elder — said: We were with Tawus at the Maqam when we heard a commotion. He asked, ""What is this?"" It was said, ""People whom Ibn Hisham seized for some offense, and he is parading them."" Then I heard Tawus narrate from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""There is no one who innovates in this community an innovation that did not exist, but he will die only after it befalls him.""** Bishr said, ""Then I saw Ibn Hisham when he was deposed and al-Walid's officials were appointed, and they paraded him."""
"10510","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the feeble-minded until he recovers, and from the child until he understands""** — or, the narrator doubted — **""until he reaches puberty.""**"
"10511","Abu Idris al-Khawlani said: More than one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me — among them Shaddad ibn Aws and Thawban (may Allah be pleased with them both) — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The pen is lifted in the fixed penalty from the child until he grows, from the sleeper until he wakes, from the insane until he recovers, and from the helpless feeble-minded.""**"
"10512","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The pen is lifted from three: from the child until he grows, from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the insane until he recovers.""**"
"10513","Aslam ibn Bajrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet placed him over the captives of Qurayzah. He would examine a boy, and if he saw that coarse hair had grown, he struck his neck; whoever had not grown hair he took and placed among the spoils of the Muslims."
"10514","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: A servant-girl belonging to the household of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed immorality, so the Prophet said: > **""O Ali, carry out the fixed penalty upon her.""** Ali left her until she delivered what was in her womb, then struck her fifty lashes. He then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned it, and the Prophet said: > **""You did right.""**"
"10515","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that a woman confessed to adultery four times while she was pregnant. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: > **""Go back until you give birth.""** She then came after she had given birth, and he said: > **""Suckle him until you wean him.""** She then came and was stoned. When she was mentioned, the Prophet said: > **""She has repented a repentance which, had the taker of unlawful tolls repented it, he would have been forgiven.""**"
"10516","Abu Said (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that a paralyzed man, chronically ill, lived near the house of Umm Sad. A woman became visibly pregnant; when asked, she said it was from him. When he was asked about it, he confessed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that he be flogged with the clustered stalks of a palm bunch."
"10517","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A man who had committed adultery was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He questioned him and the man confessed, so the Prophet ordered him stripped — and he proved to be a man of frail build. The Prophet sat and said: > **""Beating will leave nothing of this man.""** So he called for a stalk bearing a hundred twigs and struck him with it a single blow."
"10518","Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a swollen-bellied old man, yellowed, his veins prominent, who had committed adultery with a woman. The Messenger of Allah struck him with a bundle containing a hundred twigs."
"10519","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Whoever testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, his blood is sacred except in three cases: the one who abandons his religion, the married adulterer, and whoever kills a soul unjustly.""**"
"10520","Ammar ibn Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The blood of the believer is not lawful except in one of three cases: a life for a life, the married adulterer, and the apostate from faith.""**"
"10521","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Whoever strips the back of a Muslim man without right will meet Allah while He is angry with him.""**"
"10522","Ismah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The back of the believer is a sanctuary except by its right.""**"
"10523","Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: > **""Not lawful in this community are tajrid, nor madd, nor safr.""**"
"10524","Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Whoever looks at a Muslim with a look that frightens him thereby, without right, Allah will frighten him on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"10525","Amir ibn Rabiah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that a man took another man's sandals and hid them while joking. When this was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Do not frighten a Muslim, for frightening a Muslim is a grave wrong.""**"
"10526","Abu Hasan — who was present at al-Aqabah and Badr (may Allah be pleased with him) — said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man rose and forgot his sandals. Another man took them and placed them beneath himself. When the man returned he asked for his sandals, and the people said, ""We have not seen them."" He insisted they were there, and the Prophet said: > **""Then what about the fright of the believer?""** The man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I only did it in play."" The Prophet repeated two or three times: > **""Then what about the fright of the believer?""**"
"10527","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: > **""Whoever frightens a believer, it becomes binding upon Allah not to grant him security from the terrors of the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"10528","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""It is not lawful for a Muslim""** — or, the narrator doubted, **""a believer, to frighten a Muslim.""**"
"10529","Al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey when a man dozed off upon his mount. Another man took an arrow from his quiver, and when the man woke he was startled. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""It is not lawful for a man to frighten a Muslim.""**"
"10530","Sulayman ibn Surad (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that a Bedouin prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a horn alongside him, and some of the people took it. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished with the salutation, the Bedouin asked for the horn, and some of the people laughed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must never frighten a Muslim.""**"
"10531","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ""Do you feel jealousy?"" He said: > **""By Allah, indeed I feel jealousy, and Allah is more jealous than I. And part of His jealousy is that He forbade immoral deeds.""**"
"10532","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: > **""I am holding you by your waists, saying: beware of Hell, beware of transgressing the fixed limits; beware of Hell, beware of transgressing the fixed limits; beware of Hell, beware of transgressing the fixed limits — three times. When I die I will leave you, and I am your forerunner at the Pool; whoever comes to it will succeed.""**"
"10533","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Beware of adultery, for in it are four traits: it removes radiance from the face, cuts off provision, angers the Most Merciful, and brings eternity in the Fire.""**"
"10534","Abd Allah ibn Busr (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: > **""Indeed the adulterers will come with their faces blazing with fire.""**"
"10535","Abd Allah ibn Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: > **""O lamented Arabs, O lamented Arabs: what I fear most for you is adultery and hidden lust.""**"
"10536","Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Three will not enter Paradise: the aged adulterer, the lying ruler, and the insolent pauper.""**"
"10537","Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""When the people of the covenant are wronged, power passes to the enemy. When adultery becomes widespread, captivity becomes widespread. And when the deed of the people of Lut becomes widespread, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, lifts His hand from creation and cares not in which valley they perish.""**"
"10538","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not look on the Day of Resurrection at the aged adulterer, nor at the aged adulteress.""**"
"10539","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Allah will not look at the grey-haired adulterer, nor at the insolent pauper.""**"
"10540","Nafi, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""There will not enter Paradise an arrogant pauper, nor an aged adulterer, nor one who reminds Allah, the Exalted, of his deeds as a favor.""**"
"10541","Buraydah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The seven heavens and the seven earths curse the aged adulterer, and the foul odor of the private parts of adulterers torments the people of the Fire."
"10542","Buraydah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it: > **""The seven heavens and the seven earths curse the aged adulterer.""**"
"10543","Abd Allah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: > **""The two eyes commit adultery, the two feet commit adultery, and the private part commits adultery.""** In Abu Yala's wording he added: > **""And the two hands commit adultery.""**"
"10544","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: > **""Every eye commits adultery.""**"
"10545","Muhammad ibn Mutarrif said: My grandfather narrated to me that he heard Alqamah, among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The adultery of the two eyes is the look.""**"
"10546","Sahl ibn Abi Umamah reported that he and his father visited Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) in the time of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, when Anas was a governor, and Anas prayed a light prayer, as though the prayer of a traveler or close to it. When he finished, Sahl's father said, ""May Allah have mercy on you, was that the prescribed prayer or something voluntary you prayed?"" Anas said, ""It was the prescribed prayer, and it is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I missed nothing of it except something I forgot."" He said the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Do not be hard upon yourselves, lest hardship be imposed upon you. For a people were hard upon themselves, so Allah imposed hardship upon them; those are their remnants in the monasteries and cloisters — a monasticism they invented which We did not prescribe for them.""** The next morning they said, ""Shall we ride out to look and reflect?"" He said, ""Yes."" So they all rode until they came upon deserted cloisters whose people had perished and vanished, left empty upon their roofs. They asked, ""Do you know these dwellings?"" He said, ""How well I know them and their people. These are the people of dwellings whom rebellion and envy destroyed. Envy extinguishes the light of good deeds, and rebellion either confirms that or belies it. The eye commits adultery, as do the palm, the foot, the hand, and the tongue, and the private part either confirms that or belies it."""
"10547","Al-Shaʿbi reported concerning the verse {If you are given this, take it, but if you are not given it, beware} [Al-Maʾidah: 41]: He mentioned the two sons of Suriya when the Prophet ﷺ came to them and said to them: > **""By the One Who revealed the Torah to Musa, and the One Who parted the sea, and the One Who sent down upon you manna and quails — do you know best?""** They said: Our people have granted us this concession. Then one of them said: He is adjuring us with such solemn matters. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""You find that the glance is zina, and the embrace is zina, and the kiss is zina.""** Then the narrator mentioned the rest of the hadith as before."
"10548","Wathilah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Intimate relations between women are zina between them.""** In the wording of Abu Yaʿla, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The intimate act of women with one another is zina.""**"
"10549","ʿAʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, meaning the child of zina: > **""He is the worst of the three if he acts according to the deed of his two parents.""**"
"10550","Ibn ʿAbbas رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The child of zina is the worst of the three if he acts according to the deed of his two parents.""**"
"10551","Maymunah, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, رضي الله عنها said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""My ummah will remain upon good so long as children of zina do not spread among them; when children of zina spread among them, it is imminent that Allah will envelop them all in punishment.""** In another wording: My ummah will remain upon good, its affair held together, so long as such does not appear among them."
"10552","ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: > **""The disobedient to parents will not enter Paradise, nor the habitual drinker of wine, nor the one who reminds others of his favors, nor the child of zina.""**"
"10553","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The child of zina will not enter Paradise, nor anything of his offspring up to seven forefathers.""**"
"10554","ʿAʾishah رضي الله عنها reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: > **""Upon the child of zina there is nothing of the sin of his two parents.""** Then he recited: {No bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another} [Al-Anʿam: 164]."
"10555","Abu al-Walid al-Qurashi said: I was with Bilal ibn Abi Burdah when a man from ʿAbd al-Qays came and said: May Allah set right the amir; the people of al-Taff do not pay zakah on their wealth. Bilal asked what had happened. The man said he knew it and had informed the amir. Bilal asked from whom he was, and of his name, and wrote to his chief of police to inquire about the man's lineage among ʿAbd al-Qays. The messenger returned and said his lineage was impugned. Bilal said: Allah is Greatest. My father narrated to me from my grandfather Abu Musa that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""None seeks out the faults of people against them except a child of adultery, or one in whom there is a trace of it.""** Abu al-Walid narrated ""yasʿa"" in place of ""yabghi."""
"10556","ʿAmr ibn Shurahbil ibn Saʿid ibn Saʿd ibn ʿUbadah reported from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Saʿd is jealous, and I am more jealous than him, and Allah is more jealous than me.""** A man asked: Over what is Allah jealous? He ﷺ said: > **""Over a man striving in the path of Allah whose family is betrayed in his absence.""**"
"10557","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Beware of the women of the warriors.""**"
"10558","Abu Qatadah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever sits upon the bed of a woman whose husband is absent, Allah will assign a serpent over him on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"10559","ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما raised it as a prophetic report, saying: > **""The likeness of one who sits upon the bed of an absent woman is like one bitten by a black serpent among the serpents of the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"10560","ʿAbdullah — meaning Ibn Masʿud رضي الله عنه — narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Let people pardon one another concerning the hudud so long as they are not raised to the rulers; when they are raised to the rulers, judgment between them is by the Book of Allah.""**"
"10561","Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah reported from his maternal aunt, the sister of Masʿud ibn al-ʿAjmaʾ, that her father said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the Makhzumiyyah woman who stole a velvet cloak: We will ransom her with forty uqiyyahs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""That she be purified is better for her.""** Then he ordered concerning her and her hand was cut. She was from Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, or from Banu Asad."
"10562","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reported that Quraysh were troubled by the affair of the Makhzumiyyah woman who stole. They asked who would speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about her, and they spoke to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Those before you were destroyed only because when the noble among them stole they left him, and when the weak among them stole they established the hadd upon him. By Allah, had Fatimah bint Muhammad done so, I would have cut off her hand.""**"
"10563","ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr reported from his father that al-Zubayr رضي الله عنه met a thief and interceded for him. It was said to him: Wait until we bring him to the ruler. He said, as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When the matter reaches the ruler, may Allah curse the intercessor and the one interceded for.""**"
"10564","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whose intercession stands in the way of a hadd from among the hudud of Allah has opposed Allah in His sovereignty.""** This has preceded in the Book of Judgments."
"10565","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whose intercession stands in the way of a hadd from among the hudud of Allah has opposed Allah in His command.""**"
"10566","Abu al-Dardaʾ رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: > **""Whatever man whose intercession stands in the way of a hadd from among the hudud of Allah remains in the anger of Allah until he withdraws.""** The complete version is in the Book of Judgments."
"10567","Abu Matar said: I saw ʿAli رضي الله عنه when a man was brought to him and it was said he had stolen a camel. ʿAli said: I do not think you stole? He said: Yes. ʿAli said: Perhaps it was confused for you? He insisted he had stolen. ʿAli said: O Qunbur, take him, bind his fingers, kindle a fire, and call the butcher to cut him, then wait until I come to you. When ʿAli came he asked: Did you steal? He said: No. So ʿAli left him. They asked: O Commander of the Faithful, why did you leave him when he had confessed to you? He said: I seized him by his word and I release him by his word. Then ʿAli said: A man who had stolen was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered his cutting, then he wept. It was asked: O Messenger of Allah, why do you weep? He said: > **""How can I not weep, when my ummah is being cut among you?""** They said: O Messenger of Allah, would you not pardon him? He said: > **""That is an evil ruler who pardons concerning the hudud; but pardon one another among yourselves.""**"
"10568","ʿAli — meaning Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه — narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever insults the Prophets is killed, and whoever insults my Companions is flogged.""**"
"10569","Kaʿb ibn ʿAlqamah reported that ʿArfah ibn al-Harith رضي الله عنه — who had companionship and fought with ʿIkrimah ibn Abi Jahl in Yemen during the Riddah — was passed by a Christian from Egypt called al-Mandaqun. ʿArfah invited him to Islam, but the Christian mentioned the Prophet ﷺ and reviled him. The matter was raised to ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAs, who summoned them and said: We have given them a covenant. ʿArfah said: Allah forbid that covenants should mean they harm us concerning Allah and His Messenger. We covenanted only to leave them and their churches alone so they may say therein what they wish, not to burden them beyond capacity, to fight on their behalf, and to leave them to their own laws unless they come to us, in which case we judge between them by what Allah revealed. ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAs said: > **""You have spoken the truth.""**"
"10570","ʿUmayr ibn Umayyah رضي الله عنه had a sister who, when he went out to the Prophet ﷺ, harmed him concerning the Prophet and insulted the Prophet ﷺ, and she was a polytheist. One day he concealed a sword for her, came to her, placed it upon her, and killed her. Her sons rose crying: We know who killed her — is our mother to be killed, when there are people whose fathers and mothers are polytheists? When ʿUmayr feared they would kill one other than her killer, he went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. The Prophet ﷺ asked: > **""Did you kill your sister?""** He said: Yes. He asked: > **""And why?""** He said: She used to harm me concerning you. The Prophet ﷺ sent for her sons, questioned them, and they named one other than her killer. The Prophet ﷺ informed them of ʿUmayr and declared her blood void. They said: Hearing and obeying."
"10571","Muʿadh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Indeed the most hateful of creation to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is one who believed and then disbelieved.""**"
"10572","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever changes his religion, kill him.""**"
"10573","ʿAʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever changes his religion, kill him.""** Muʿawiyah ibn Haydah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever changes his religion, kill him. Allah does not accept the repentance of a servant who disbelieves after his Islam.""**"
"10574","ʿIsmah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever changes his religion, kill him.""**"
"10575","ʿAbd al-Rahman ibn Thawban reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in his sermon: > **""This town — meaning Madinah — is not fit for two qiblas therein; whichever Christian embraces Islam then returns to Christianity, strike his neck.""**"
"10576","Abu Musa and Muʿadh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent them to Yemen and ordered them to teach people the Qurʾan. Muʿadh came visiting Abu Musa and found with him a man bound in iron. Muʿadh said: O my brother, were we sent to punish people? We were sent to teach them their religion and command them to what benefits them. Abu Musa said: He embraced Islam then disbelieved. Muʿadh said: > **""By the One Who sent Muhammad with the truth, I will not move until I burn him with fire.""** Abu Musa said there remained something with him, but Muʿadh swore he would not move. Firewood was brought, fire kindled, the man bound and cast in."
"10577","Qays ibn Abi Hazim said: A man came to Ibn Masʿud رضي الله عنه and said: I passed a mosque of Banu Hanifah and heard them reciting what Allah never revealed: ""The grinders grinding, the bakers baking, the kneaders kneading, the morsel-makers morseling."" Ibn Masʿud brought forth Ibn al-Nawwahah, their imam, and killed him, but deemed the rest too many. He said: > **""I will not hand them over to Satan today; march them to Sham until Allah grants them repentance or the plague annihilates them.""** Then the narrator mentioned the hadith."
"10578","Al-Qasim said: A man came to ʿAbdullah — meaning Ibn Masʿud رضي الله عنه — and said: O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, here are people reciting the recitation of Musaylimah. ʿAbdullah sent him back. After some time the man returned and swore he had just left them in a house with that codex among them. ʿAbdullah commanded Qarazah ibn Kaʿb to march with the people and bring them. When brought, ʿAbdullah asked: What is this, after Islam has spread? They said: O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, we seek Allah's forgiveness, repent to Him, and testify that Musaylimah is the liar who fabricated against Allah and His Messenger. ʿAbdullah sought their repentance and marched them to Sham — nearly eighty men. Ibn al-Nawwahah refused to repent, so Qarazah ibn Kaʿb by order took him to the market, struck his neck, and ordered his head be cast into his mother's lap. ʿAbd al-Rahman ibn ʿAbdullah said: I later met an elder of them in Sham who told me: > **""May Allah have mercy upon your father; by Allah, had he killed us that day, we would all have entered the Fire.""**"
"10579","Suwayd ibn Ghaflah reported that ʿAli رضي الله عنه learned that people in Basrah had apostatized. He sent provisions to them for two weeks, then called them to Islam and they refused. He dug a pit for them, stood over it, and said: > **""I shall surely fill you with fat and flesh.""** Then they were brought, their necks struck, cast into the pit, firewood cast over them and burned. Then ʿAli said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. Suwayd followed him when he left and asked about his saying. ʿAli replied: Woe to you, around me are ignorant people; when you hear me say the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, then falling from heaven is dearer to me than to attribute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he did not say."
"10580","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه said: Nabhan apostatized three times, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""O Allah, grant me power over Nabhan with a black rope upon his neck.""** He turned and there was Nabhan seized with a black rope on his neck. They brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the sword in his right hand and the rope in his left to kill him. A man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, would you step aside from it? So he handed the sword to a man and said: > **""Go and strike his neck.""** As he was taken, Nabhan laughed and said: Would you kill a man who testifies there is no deity but Allah and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? So he was released."
"10581","Jabir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought the repentance of a man who apostatized from Islam four times. > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought his repentance four times.""**"
"10582","Ibn ʿAbbas رضي الله عنهما reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: > **""Whose religion departs from the religion of Islam, strike his neck.""** And he said: > **""If he testifies there is no deity but Allah and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, there is no way against him, unless he commits something for which its hadd is established upon him.""**"
"10583","Muʿadh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him when he sent him to Yemen: > **""Whatever man apostatizes from Islam, invite him; if he repents, accept it from him, and if he does not repent, strike his neck. And whatever woman apostatizes from Islam, invite her; if she repents, accept it from her, and if she refuses, keep seeking her repentance.""**"
"10584","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said: We used to say: What repentance is there for one tempted who abandons his religion after his Islam and knowledge? Then Allah revealed concerning them: {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah} [Az-Zumar: 53]. Then he mentioned the hadith, which has preceded in the Book of Hijrah. > **""O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah.""**"
"10585","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Ihsan is of two kinds: the ihsan of chastity, and the ihsan of marriage.""**"
"10586","Ibn ʿAbbas رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A day under a just imam is better than worship of sixty years, and a hadd established in the land in its right is more purifying than rain for forty mornings.""**"
"10587","Ibn ʿAbbas رضي الله عنهما said concerning His saying {As for those of your women who commit indecency} [An-Nisaʾ: 15]: They used to be confined in houses; if she died, she died, and if she lived, she lived — until this verse in An-Nur was revealed: {The adulteress and the adulterer, flog each of them one hundred lashes} [An-Nur: 2]. Then the chapter of hudud was revealed, so whoever did anything was flogged and released. > **""The adulteress and the adulterer, flog each of them one hundred lashes.""**"
"10588","ʿUbadah ibn al-Samit رضي الله عنه said: There was revealed upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: {As for those of your women who commit indecency} [An-Nisaʾ: 15] to the end of the verse, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acted accordingly with them. While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat with us around him — when revelation descended he turned away from us and we turned away from him, his face changed color and he was distressed — then when revelation was lifted he said: > **""Take from me. Allah has made a way for them: the virgin with the virgin — one hundred lashes and exile for a year; the married with the married — one hundred lashes, then stoning.""** Al-Hasan said: I do not know if it is part of the hadith or not, that he said: > **""If they testify they were found in one blanket without witnessing intercourse, they are flogged one hundred and their heads shaved.""**"
"10589","Qabisah ibn Hurayth reported from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbiq رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Take from me, take from me. Allah has made a way for them: the virgin with the virgin — one hundred lashes and exile for a year; the married with the married — one hundred lashes and stoning.""**"
"10590","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned, and Abu Bakr and ʿUmar stoned, and their command is sunnah. > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned, and Abu Bakr and ʿUmar stoned.""**"
"10591","ʿUbadah ibn al-Samit رضي الله عنه said: When the verse of stoning was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while among his Companions — when revelation descended it seized him like slumber, then when it ended he sat upright and said: > **""Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has made a way for them: the married with the married — one hundred lashes and stoning; the virgin with the virgin — one hundred lashes and exile for a year.""** Some said to Saʿd ibn ʿUbadah: O Abu Thabit, the hudud have been revealed; what if you found a man with your wife? He said: I would strike them with the sword until they are still. Am I to gather four witnesses while the wretch finishes his need, then return saying I saw such-and-such, only to be flogged and my testimony never accepted? The people laughed and gathered before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reporting Saʿd's words. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The sword suffices as a witness.""** Then he said: > **""Were it not that I fear the intoxicated and the jealous would follow suit in it.""** They said he is the most jealous of men. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""He is severely jealous, and I am more jealous than him, and Allah is more jealous than me; for that reason He ordained the hudud.""**"
"10592","Al-ʿAjmaʾ رضي الله عنها said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""The old man and the old woman, when they commit zina, stone them outright for the pleasure they enjoyed.""**"
"10593","ʿAbdullah — meaning Ibn Masʿud رضي الله عنه — said concerning the virgin who commits zina with a virgin: > **""They are both flogged one hundred lashes and exiled for a year.""**"
"10594","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I do not know whether the hudud are expiations or not.""**"
"10595","Khuzaymah ibn Thabit رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whatever servant commits something Allah forbade, then its hadd is established upon him, it expiates that sin from him.""**"
"10596","In a narration: > **""Whoever commits a sin and the hadd for that sin is established upon him, it is his expiation.""**"
"10597","The same expiation report was also narrated as mawquf, stopped at a Companion and not raised to the Prophet ﷺ. > **""Whoever commits a sin and its hadd is established upon him, it is his expiation.""**"
"10598","Khuzaymah ibn Muʿammar al-Ansari رضي الله عنه said: A woman was stoned in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and people said her deeds were nullified. When that reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: > **""It is expiation for her sins, and she shall be resurrected apart from that.""**"
"10599","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No man is punished for a sin except that Allah makes it an expiation for what he committed of that sin.""**"
"10600","Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi رضي الله عنه said: While I was in a garden of Madinah I saw a woman, and I had no concern but her until she passed me; I kept following her with my gaze until I reached the wall, then I turned and the wall struck my face and bloodied me. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he said: > **""When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intends good for a servant, He hastens the punishment of his sin for him in this world; and our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, is too noble to punish twice for one sin.""**"
"10601","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A man's being killed in captivity is expiation for his prior sins.""**"
"10602","ʿAʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Death in captivity does not pass by any sin except that it erases it.""**"
"10603","Ibn Masʿud رضي الله عنه said concerning one who incurs hudud then is killed deliberately: > **""When killing comes, everything is erased.""**"
"10604","Al-Hasan said: Ziyad used to pursue the partisans of ʿAli and kill them. When that reached al-Hasan ibn ʿAli رضي الله عنهما, he said: > **""O Allah, single him out with a natural death, for killing is expiation.""**"
"10605","Abu Bakr — meaning al-Siddiq رضي الله عنه — said: I sat with the Prophet ﷺ when Maʿiz ibn Malik came and confessed once, and he turned him away; then he confessed a second time, and he turned him away; then he confessed a third time, and he turned him away. I said to him: If you confess a fourth time, he will stone you. So he confessed a fourth time, and the Prophet ﷺ detained him, inquired about him, and they said: We know only good. Then he ordered his stoning. In the wording of al-Bazzar: The Prophet ﷺ turned Maʿiz away four times, then ordered his stoning. > **""The Prophet ﷺ turned Maʿiz away four times, then ordered his stoning.""**"
"10606","Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came and said: The wretched one has committed zina. The Prophet turned away, then the man repeated it a third and fourth time. The Prophet ﷺ dismounted — once the narrator said the man affirmed adultery before him — and he turned him away four times. Then he dismounted, ordered us, and we dug a pit not deep, and the man was stoned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed grieved and sorrowful; we marched until we halted, and his distress was lifted. He said to me: > **""O Abu Dharr, have you not seen your companion — he has been forgiven and admitted to Paradise.""**"
"10607","Ibn ʿAbbas رضي الله عنهما said: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed people on Friday, a man of Banu Layth ibn Bakr ibn ʿAbd Manah ibn Kinanah came stepping over people until he drew near and said: O Messenger of Allah, establish the hadd upon me. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Sit down.""** He sat, then stood a second time and a third, and the Prophet ﷺ said the same. He asked: > **""And what is your hadd?""** The man said: I approached a forbidden woman. The Prophet ﷺ said to men among his Companions — among them ʿAli ibn Abi Talib, al-ʿAbbas, Zayd ibn Harithah, and ʿUthman ibn ʿAffan رضي الله عنهم: > **""Take him and flog him one hundred lashes.""** The Laythi had never married. They asked: O Messenger of Allah, will you not flog the woman with whom he sinned? The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Bring him to me after flogging.""** When brought, the Prophet ﷺ asked: > **""Who is your companion?""** He named a woman of Banu Bakr. She was brought and questioned, but said: By Allah he lies; I do not know him, I am innocent of what he says, and Allah is witness to what I say. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Who testifies that you sinned with her? She denies. If you have witnesses, I shall flog her with the hadd; otherwise I shall flog you with the hadd of slander.""** He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have none to testify. So he ordered him flogged eighty for slander."
"10608","ʿAbd al-ʿAziz ibn ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr al-Qurashi reported from one who witnessed the Prophet ﷺ: The Prophet ordered the stoning of a man between Makkah and Madinah. When the stones struck him, he fled. When that reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: > **""Why did you not leave him?""**"
"10609","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: > **""When a man confesses to zina and the stoning overtakes him, then he flees, he is left.""** In al-Tirmidhi concerning Maʿiz: > **""Why did you not leave him?""**"
"10610","Jabir ibn Samurah رضي الله عنه said: Maʿiz ibn Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed zina. The Prophet turned his face away, then the man came from the front and he turned away, then a third and fourth time. When he repeated it, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his Companions: > **""Rise to your companion; if he is sound, then stone him.""** They inquired and found him sound, so he was stoned. When the stones struck him he rushed among them, and a Companion met him with a camel's jawbone, struck him, and killed him. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: To the Fire. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No; he has repented a repentance which, had a nation among nations repented it, it would have been accepted from them.""**"
"10611","Sahl ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنه said: I witnessed Maʿiz when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered his stoning and he ran; people followed stoning him until ʿUmar met him at al-Jabbanah and struck him with a camel's jawbone, killing him. > **""I witnessed Maʿiz when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered his stoning.""**"
"10612","Abu Barzah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned Maʿiz ibn Malik. > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned Maʿiz ibn Malik.""**"
"10613","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, there is a developing life in my belly, so establish the hadd upon me. He said: > **""We do not kill what is in your belly.""** She left; when she gave birth she returned and said: I have given birth. He said: > **""Go and nurse him until you wean him.""** When she weaned him she came and said: I have weaned him, O Messenger of Allah. He said: > **""Go and provide a guardian for him.""** She left, then returned walking with her sister. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ marveled at her patience and ordered her stoning. Then the Prophet ﷺ said to a man: > **""Go, and when she is placed in her pit, stand before her so you are before her eyes, and whisper to her.""** And he ordered another man: > **""Go to a large stone, come to her from behind, cast it, and crush her.""**"
"10614","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reported that a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ, said she had committed zina, and was pregnant. He said: > **""Go until you deliver your burden.""** Had she not returned, he would not have sent for her. She delivered, then came to him. He said: > **""Go until you wean your child.""** She came to him — had she not come, he would not have sent for her — and after weaning him she came, and he had her stoned."
"10615","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ, confessed zina, and was pregnant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed her until she gave birth, then ordered her garments bound upon her, ordered her stoning, and prayed over her. A man asked: Do you pray over her when she committed zina and you stoned her? The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""She has repented a repentance which, had seventy of the people of Madinah repented it, it would have been accepted from them. Have you found any better than one who sacrificed herself?""**"
"10616","Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ stoned a woman and ordered him to dig for her, so he dug for her up to his navel. > **""The Prophet ﷺ stoned a woman, and I dug for her up to my navel.""**"
"10617","Salih ibn Rashid al-Qurashi said: A man who had assaulted his own sister was brought to al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf. Al-Hajjaj said: Detain him and ask the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ here. They asked ʿAbdullah ibn Abi Mutarrif, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever crosses the two sacred bounds, split his middle with the sword.""** They wrote to ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAbbas, and he wrote back the like of ʿAbdullah ibn Abi Mutarrif's saying."
"10618","Al-Baraʾ ibn ʿAzib رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ sent against a man who had married his father's wife that he be killed. In another wording: Strike his neck and bring his head. > **""The Prophet ﷺ sent against a man who married his father's wife that he be killed.""**"
"10619","Mutarrif said: They came to a dome, brought forth a man, and killed him. I asked: What is this? They said: This is a man who consummated with his wife's mother, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent against him and they killed him. > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent against him, and they killed him.""**"
"10620","Ibn ʿAbbas رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever approaches a mahram woman will not enter Paradise.""**"
"10621","ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: > **""Whoever approaches a mahram woman will not enter Paradise.""**"
"10622","On the authority of Ma'bad and Ubayd, the two sons of Imran ibn Dhuhl, who both said: a man was brought to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) and confessed, I have committed zina. Ibn Mas'ud said that he would then be stoned if he were muhṣan. Those present explained that he had gone in to his wife's slave-girl, jariya. Abdullah ruled that if he had coerced her, ikrah, he must free her and give his wife another slave-girl in her place. The man swore by Allah that he had coerced and beaten her, so Ibn Mas'ud did not have him stoned but ordered a beating less than the ḥadd. > **""If you coerced her, then free her, and give your wife a slave-girl in her place.""**"
"10623","On the authority of al-Sha'bi, that Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) held the view that there is upon such a man neither ḥadd nor dower, 'uqr. That is, one who goes in to his wife's slave-girl incurs no fixed punishment and no compensatory dower under this ruling. > **""There is no ḥadd upon him, nor dower.""**"
"10624","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: there is no ḥadd upon the slave-girl, ama, until she attains iḥṣan. When she attains iḥṣan through marriage, zawaj, then upon her is half of what is upon the free muḥṣanat. > **""There is no ḥadd upon the slave-girl until she becomes muḥṣana, then when she becomes muḥṣana through a husband, upon her is half of what is upon the muḥṣanat.""**"
"10625","On the authority of Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, that Ma'qil ibn Muqarrin al-Muzani (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) and said that a slave-girl of his had committed zina. Abdullah ordered him to flog her fifty, jald. When Ma'qil objected that she had no husband, Abdullah replied that her Islam is her iḥṣan. > **""Flog her fifty; her Islam is her iḥṣan.""**"
"10626","On the authority of Abu Juḥayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warded off the ḥadd from a woman who had been coerced, mustakraha. Coercion removes culpability, so no fixed punishment falls upon her. > **""The ḥadd is warded off from her.""**"
"10627","On the authority of Abd al-Karim, as conveyed from Ali ibn Abi Talib and Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them), concerning the virgin, bikr, coerced against herself: for the virgin is the like of the dower, ṣadaq, of one of her peers among women, and for the previously married woman, thayyib, is the like of the dower of her peers. > **""For the virgin is like the dower of one of her women, and for the thayyib is like the dower of her peers.""**"
"10628","On the authority of Abd al-Karim, that Ali and Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them) both said concerning the slave-girl, ama, who is coerced: if she was a virgin, bikr, then a tenth of her price, 'ushr thaman, and if she was thayyib, then half a tenth of her price. > **""If she was a virgin, a tenth of her price, and if she was thayyib, half a tenth of her price.""**"
"10629","On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: a man found with a woman under one blanket, liḥaf, was brought to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him). Abdullah had each of them struck forty lashes, sawt, and stood them before the people. Their families complained to Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), who asked Ibn Mas'ud whether this was his considered judgment, ra'y. When he confirmed it, Umar approved it as excellent judgment. > **""Yes, it is my judgment.""**"
"10630","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the stoning, rajm, of a Jewish man and Jewish woman at the door of the mosque. When the man felt the stones he rose over his companion to shield her from them until both were killed. Thus Allah vindicated His Messenger in the establishment of zina against them. > **""Stone them.""**"
"10631","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that a group came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a woman and asked what had been revealed to him about zina. He told them to bring two learned men of Banu Isra'il. They brought a young eloquent man and an old man whose eyebrows fell over his eyes. Adjured by Allah who sent the Torah to Musa (peace be upon him), they confessed that Allah revealed stoning for the adulterer, but their people, full of youths and beautiful women, had abandoned it for flogging and shaming, ta'zir. The Prophet ordered the woman taken away and stoned after she delivered what was in her womb. > **""Go and bring me two men from the scholars of Banu Isra'il.""**"
"10632","On the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Jews brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a Jewish man and Jewish woman who had committed zina while both were muḥṣan. The Messenger ordered them stoned, and the narrator said he was among those who stoned them. > **""Stone them.""**"
"10633","On the authority of Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: the Jews brought a man and woman who had committed zina. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told them to bring their two most learned men, so they brought the two sons of Ṣuriya. He asked whether they were the most learned behind them, and they said so it is claimed. He adjured them by Allah who sent the Torah to Musa about Allah's ruling: they answered that mere seclusion in a house or garment or upon her body is suspicion, riba, with discretionary punishment, 'uquba, but stoning requires four witnesses to penetration like the kohl stick in its case, mil fi mukḥula. Asked why they did not stone, they said their authority had gone and they disliked killing. The Prophet summoned the witnesses, they testified, and he ordered stoning. > **""Bring me the two most learned men among you.""**"
"10634","On the authority of Jabir, who heard Salim ibn Abdullah, Aban ibn Uthman, and Zayd ibn Hasan relate: a man who had committed foul sodomy, fujur, with a well-born Qurashi boy was brought to Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him). Uthman demanded witnesses and asked about iḥṣan. They said he had married a woman but not yet consummated with her, dukhul. Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both) told Uthman that consummation would have made stoning due, but without it the man is flogged with the ḥadd. Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) testified that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say what Abu al-Hasan had said, so Uthman ordered one hundred lashes. > **""If he had entered with her, stoning would have become due; since he has not entered with his wife, flog him the ḥadd.""**"
"10635","On the authority of Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: three are such that their testimony that there is no god but Allah is not accepted: the active and passive male partners in sodomy, rakib and markub, the active and passive female partners, rakiba and markuba, and the unjust ruler, imam ja'ir. > **""Three whose testimony that there is no god but Allah is not accepted: the rider and the ridden, the female rider and the ridden, and the unjust ruler.""**"
"10636","On the authority of Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed seven of His creation from above His seven heavens, repeating the curse thrice upon one though one curse would suffice each. Cursed is whoever does the act of the people of Lut, repeated thrice; cursed is whoever slaughters for other than Allah; cursed is whoever goes in to an animal, bahima; cursed is whoever disobeys his parents, 'uquq; cursed is whoever joins a woman and her daughter; cursed is whoever alters the boundaries of land; cursed is whoever ascribes himself to other than his patrons, mawali. > **""Cursed is whoever does the act of the people of Lut, cursed is whoever does the act of the people of Lut, cursed is whoever does the act of the people of Lut.""**"
"10637","On the authority of Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: four wake in Allah's anger, ghaḍab, and sleep in His displeasure, sakhat. Asked who they are, Messenger of Allah, he named men imitating women, mutashabbihun, women imitating men, mutashabbihat, one who goes in to an animal, and one who goes in to men. > **""The men who imitate women, the women who imitate men, the one who goes in to an animal, and the one who goes in to men.""**"
"10638","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), that an effeminate man, mukhannath, with hands and feet dyed with henna, khiḍab, was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Companions began striking him with their sandals. The Prophet ordered them to guard their women from him and his fellows. When they asked whether to kill him, he refused, saying he had been forbidden to kill those who pray, muṣallin. > **""Beware of him and his fellows for your women; no, I have been forbidden from killing those who pray.""**"
"10639","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed effeminate men, mukhannathin, and said: expel them from your houses, buyut. > **""Expel them from your houses.""**"
"10640","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he cursed ten: the woman who tattoos, washima, and the one tattooed, mawshuma, the woman who plucks her face, saliqa, the woman who joins hair, waṣila, and the one joined, mawṣula, the eater of riba and its witness, the withholder of charity, ṣadaqa, the man imitating women, and the woman imitating men. > **""Allah has cursed the tattooer and the tattooed, and those who imitate.""**"
"10641","On the authority of Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: whoever falls upon an animal, bahima, kill him and kill it with him. > **""Whoever falls upon an animal, kill him and kill it with him.""**"
"10642","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: there is no amputation, qat', for less than ten dirhams. > **""There is no amputation for less than ten dirhams.""**"
"10643","On the authority of Irak, who heard Marwan at the pilgrimage season, mawsim, say: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) amputated for a shield, mijann, and a camel is more valuable than a shield. The point is that the threshold was plainly met. > **""The Messenger of Allah amputated for a shield, and a camel is better than a shield.""**"
"10644","On the authority of Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: the hand is not cut except for a dinar or ten dirhams. This is a suspended ruling, mawquf, of the Companion on the minimum value, niṣab. > **""The hand is not cut except for a dinar or ten dirhams.""**"
"10645","On the authority of Zaḥr ibn Rabi'a, that Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: amputation is for a dinar or ten dirhams. > **""Amputation is for a dinar or ten dirhams.""**"
"10646","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: there is no amputation except for ten dirhams. > **""There is no amputation except for ten dirhams.""**"
"10647","On the authority of Umm Ayman (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: the thief is not cut except for a shield, jaḥfa. It was valued in the time of the Messenger at a dinar or ten dirhams. > **""The thief is not cut except for a shield.""**"
"10648","On the authority of Sa'd, meaning Ibn Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) amputated for a shield, mijann, whose price was five dirhams. > **""He amputated for a shield.""**"
"10649","On the authority of Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) amputated for an iron egg-shaped helm, bayḍa, whose value was twenty-one dirhams. > **""He amputated for an iron helm.""**"
"10650","On the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that a slave-girl stole a skin of wine, zukra, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) worth less than three dirhams, and the Prophet did not have her cut. > **""He did not cut her.""**"
"10651","On the authority of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: there is no amputation for grazing livestock, mashiya, except what is beyond the pen, zirb, nor for dates, tamr, except what has reached the storehouse, jarin. > **""There is no amputation for livestock except what is beyond the pen, nor for dates except what the storehouse has sheltered.""**"
"10652","On the authority of Hammam ibn al-Harith, that Ibn Muqarrin asked Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I swore not to sleep upon a bed for a year. Abdullah recited the verse, O you who believe, do not forbid the good things Allah has made lawful for you, and told him to expiate his oath, kaffara, and sleep upon his bed. When he said he was wealthy, Abdullah told him to free a slave, raqaba. When he said his slave stole a cloak, qaba, from him, Abdullah said his own wealth had stolen part from part, so no amputation. When he said his slave-girl committed zina, Abdullah told him to flog her; to the plea she was not muḥṣana he answered that her Islam is her iḥṣan. > **""Expiate your oath and sleep upon your bed; her Islam is her iḥṣan.""**"
"10653","On the authority of al-Qasim, who said: a slave-girl who had stolen and was not muḥṣana was brought to Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he did not have her cut. > **""He did not cut her.""**"
"10654","On the authority of al-Qasim also, who said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), arrived after Sa'd had built the palace and taken a mosque among the companions of al-Namir, going out to it for prayers. When Abdullah took charge of the public treasury, bayt al-mal, it was broken into and he seized the man. He wrote to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and Umar wrote back not to cut him, but to move the mosque and place the treasury toward the qibla, since someone praying remains in the mosque. Abdullah moved it and drew this plan. Sa'd's palace had a raised ledge, shadharwan, upon which the imam stood, so Abdullah ordered it demolished until the imam's standing was level with the people. > **""Do not cut him; move the mosque and place the treasury toward the qibla.""**"
"10655","On the authority of Isma (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: a slave stole in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and was brought, and he pardoned him; brought a second time stealing, he pardoned; a third time, he pardoned; a fourth time, he pardoned. Brought a fifth time stealing, he cut his hand; a sixth time, he cut his foot; a seventh time, he cut his hand; an eighth time, he cut his foot. And the Messenger said: four for four. > **""Four for four.""**"
"10656","On the authority of Abu Majid, meaning al-Hanafi, who said: I sat with Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who recalled the first man the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever cut: a thief was brought and his hand was cut, and the Prophet's face showed sorrow, asaf. Asked if he disliked the cutting, he asked what would prevent him, warned them not to be helpers of Satan against their brother, and taught that when a ḥadd reaches the ruler, imam, he must establish it. Allah is Pardoning and loves pardon, so let them pardon and overlook; do you not love that Allah forgive you, for Allah is Forgiving, Merciful. > **""Do not be helpers of Satan against your brother; it befits the imam when a ḥadd reaches him to establish it.""**"
"10657","In another narration from him also: the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) showed sorrow, as if ashes, ramad, had been strewn upon it, at the cutting of the thief. > **""His face changed as if ashes had been strewn upon it.""**"
"10658","In another narration: a man brought his nephew to Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) for theft, and Abdullah said: you know the first ḥadd in Islam was a woman who stole, and her hand was cut. Then he related the like of the preceding account. > **""The first ḥadd in Islam was a woman who stole, and her hand was cut.""**"
"10659","On the authority of Abu Majid al-Hanafi, who said: a man brought his drunken nephew to Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), saying he found him drunk, sukran. Abdullah told them to shake him, tartir, rouse him, mazmiz, and smell him, istinkah. They did so and found the smell of drink. Abdullah ordered him to prison, brought him out next day, ordered a whip whose fruit was beaten until lightened, mukhaffafa, and told the executioner to flog with restrained hand giving each limb its due, striking painfully but not brutally, while the man wore cloak and trousers, qaba and sarawil. Then Abdullah rebuked the uncle as an evil guardian of the orphan, neither disciplining well nor covering shame. When the uncle pleaded love like for his own child, Abdullah said Allah loves pardon, yet a ruler brought a ḥadd must establish it. Then he related from the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the first Muslim cut among the Ansar was accused of theft. > **""Shake him, rouse him, and smell him; flog him and restrain your hand, giving each limb its due.""**"
"10660","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that a woman stole in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Her victims brought her, her kin offered ransom, fidya, but the Messenger said: cut her hand. They offered five hundred dinars as ransom, he again said: cut her hand. Her right hand was cut. She asked, Messenger of Allah, is there repentance, tawba, for me. He said: yes, today you are from your sin as on the day your mother bore you. Then Allah revealed in Surat al-Ma'ida: whoever repents after his wrongdoing and reforms, Allah turns to him. > **""Cut her hand; yes, today you are from your sin as on the day your mother bore you.""**"
"10661","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that Safwan ibn Umayya came to Madina, slept in the mosque with his wrap, khamiṣa, under his head. A thief stole it and was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who ordered cutting. Safwan said, Messenger of Allah, it is his. The Prophet replied: why not before you brought him to me. > **""Why not before you brought him to me.""**"
"10662","On the authority of Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), that a thief was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said he stole. He said: I do not think he stole. The man admitted, yes, Messenger of Allah, I did. He said: take him and cut him, then cauterize him, ḥasm, then bring him to me. They cut and cauterized him and brought him. He said: repent to Allah. The man said: I repent to Allah. He said: Allah has turned to you. > **""Take him and cut him, then cauterize him, then bring him to me; repent to Allah.""**"
"10663","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Hatib, or al-Harith, who mentioned Ibn al-Zubayr's long eagerness for leadership, imara. Asked why, he said: a robber, liṣṣ, was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who ordered killing; told it was theft, he said: cut him. Later, after his extremities, qawa'im, were cut, he was brought to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said he finds for him only what the Messenger had decreed the day he ordered his killing, for he knew him best. Abu Bakr ordered some youths of the Muhajirun, among them the narrator, to kill him. Ibn al-Zubayr said: make me your commander, amir, so they did, and they took him to al-Baqi' and killed him. > **""Cut him.""**"
"10664","On the authority of Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him), that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid snatching, khilsa, and plunder, nuhba. These are open seizure, not secret theft, so no amputation but prohibition and liability. > **""He forbade snatching and plunder.""**"
"10665","In a narration from him: the word mutilation, muthla, appears instead of plunder, nuhba. Its chain contains an unnamed man. > **""He forbade snatching and mutilation.""**"
"10666","On the authority of Shuraḥbil ibn Aws (may Allah be pleased with him), who was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: whoever drinks wine, khamr, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, kill him. > **""Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, kill him.""**"
"10667","On the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Kabsha, who heard a Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relate to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan concerning wine: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning wine: if he drinks it, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns a fourth time, kill him. > **""If he drinks it, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns a fourth time, kill him.""**"
"10668","On the authority of Jarir, meaning Ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: whoever drinks wine, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns a fourth time, kill him. > **""Whoever drinks wine, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns a fourth time, kill him.""**"
"10669","On the authority of al-Sharid (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: when one of you drinks wine, strike him; if he returns, strike him; then if he returns, strike him; then if he returns a fourth time, kill him. > **""When one of you drinks wine, strike him; if he returns, strike him; then if he returns, strike him; then if he returns a fourth time, kill him.""**"
"10670","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: whoever drinks wine, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks a fourth time, kill him. Abdullah used to say: bring me a man who has drunk thrice, and I guarantee to strike his neck. > **""Whoever drinks wine, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks a fourth time, kill him.""**"
"10671","On the authority of Ghuḍayf, meaning Ibn al-Harith (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: when a man drinks wine, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, kill him. > **""When a man drinks wine, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, kill him.""**"
"10672","On the authority of Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with her), that folk of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He taught them prayer, sunan, and obligations, fara'id. They asked about a drink of wheat and barley. He asked: Ghubayra. They said yes. He said: do not taste it. When departing they asked again, he repeated it. They said they will not leave it. He said: whoever does not leave it, strike his neck. > **""Do not taste it; whoever does not leave it, strike his neck.""**"
"10673","On the authority of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that a drunkard, sakran, was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had him flogged the ḥadd. > **""He flogged him the ḥadd.""**"
"10674","Abu Ya'la related it with addition: he then asked: what is your drink. He answered: raisins and dates, zabib and tamr. That is, the intoxicant was of date and raisin brew. > **""What is your drink.""**"
"10675","On the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns a fourth time, kill him. Al-Nu'ayman was then brought having drunk a fourth time, and he flogged him without killing him, and that abrogated, nasakh, killing. > **""Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns a fourth time, kill him.""**"
"10676","On the authority of Azhar, father of Abd al-Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him), that a drinker was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar. He threw dust in his face, then ordered his Companions, who struck him with sandals and what was in their hands until he told them to stop, and that remained his practice, sunna, until he died (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Abu Bakr flogged forty for wine, Umar flogged forty early in his rule then eighty late, Uthman forty, and Mu'awiya eighty (may Allah be pleased with them). > **""Stop.""**"
"10677","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: whoever drinks a mouthful of wine, baṣqa, flog him eighty. > **""Whoever drinks a mouthful of wine, flog him eighty.""**"
"10678","On the authority of Imran ibn Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him and his father): he flogged for wine with palm stalks, jarid, and sandals, forty. This is the report of his practice. > **""He flogged forty with stalks and sandals.""**"
"10679","On the authority of Abu Ja'far, who said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) flogged a Qurashi man the ḥadd for wine, forty lashes with a whip having two ends. Abu Ja'far did not hear from Ali. > **""He flogged him forty.""**"
"10680","On the authority of Burayda (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Ma'iz ibn Malik came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who turned him away, then said: smell him, istinkihu. They smelled him, then he was stoned. Smelling here tested drink as confusion before establishing zina. > **""Smell him.""**"
"10681","On the authority of Abu Majid al-Hanafi, who said: a man brought his drunken nephew to Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), saying he found him drunk. Abdullah said: shake him, rouse him, and smell him. They shook, roused, and smelled him, finding the odor of drink. Abdullah jailed him, brought him out next day, ordered a lightened whip, told the flogger to restrain his hand and give each limb its due, striking without brutality while clothed in cloak and trousers. The full account has preceded in the chapter of theft. > **""Shake him, rouse him, and smell him.""**"
"10682","On the authority of Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: slandering the chaste woman, qadhf al-muḥṣana, demolishes the deeds of a hundred years. > **""Slandering the chaste woman demolishes the deeds of a hundred years.""**"
"10683","On the authority of Abu al-Yusr (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): O Aisha, Allah has revealed your excuse, 'udhr. She replied: by Allah's praise, not by your praise. The Messenger left Aisha, sent for Abdullah ibn Ubayy and struck him two ḥadds, then sent for Mistah and Hamna and had them struck. This concerns the slander, ifk. > **""O Aisha, Allah has revealed your excuse.""**"
"10684","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had them flogged eighty each for the slander. That is the ḥadd of qadhf. > **""He flogged them eighty each.""**"
"10685","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed concerning the child of the mutual invokers, mutala'inayn, that he inherits his mother and his mother inherits him. Whoever casts up zina to her is flogged eighty, and whoever calls him child of zina is flogged eighty. > **""He inherits his mother, and his mother inherits him; whoever slanders her is flogged eighty.""**"
"10686","On the authority of al-Qasim, who said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), said: there is no ḥadd except in two: that a chaste woman be slandered, qadhf muḥṣana, or that a man be denied from his father, nafy. > **""There is no ḥadd except in two: slandering a chaste woman, or denying a man from his father.""**"
"10687","On the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, who said: Abu Bakra, Nafi', and Shibl ibn Ma'bad testified against al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba (may Allah be pleased with them) that they saw him as one sees the kohl stick in its case, mirwad fi mukḥula. Then Ziyad came, and Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: a man has come who testifies only to truth. Ziyad said: I saw an ugly sight, manẓar qabih, and excitement, ibtihar. So Umar had them flogged the ḥadd for incomplete testimony of zina. > **""A man has come who testifies only to truth.""**"
"10688","On the authority of Wathila (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: whoever slanders a dhimmi will be bounded for him on the Day of Resurrection with whips of fire, siyat min nar. Asked of Makhul what is the severest that may be said to him, he said: it is said to him, O son of the disbeliever, ibn al-kafir. > **""Whoever slanders a dhimmi will be flogged for him on the Day of Resurrection with whips of fire.""**"
"10689","On the authority of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that a slave-girl of Hafsa, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and may Allah be pleased with her), bewitched her, siḥr, then confessed it against herself. Hafsa ordered Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid to kill her, and he did. Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) objected to her, and Abdullah explained that she had bewitched and confessed. It is as if Uthman objected to her acting without the ruler, sultan. > **""She bewitched her and confessed it.""**"
"10690","On the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: a man who entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tied knots for him, 'aqd, and cast them in an Ansari man's well. Two angels came visiting him, one sitting at his head, ra's, the other at his feet. One asked whether he knew his ailment; the other said so-and-so cast knots and threw them in so-and-so's well, and if he sent there he would find the water yellow. The Prophet sent a man who took the knots and untied them, and he recovered, bara'. The man continued to enter upon the Prophet afterward, yet he mentioned nothing of it to him nor blamed him, 'itab. > **""If he sent to it, he would find the water yellow.""**"
"10691","In another narration: a Jewish man bewitched the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he complained thereof for days. Jibril (peace be upon him) came and said: a Jewish man has bewitched you, tying knots for you. The Messenger sent Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who brought them out. With each knot untied he found lightness, khiffa. The like of the account has preceded. > **""A Jewish man has bewitched you, tying knots for you.""**"
"10692","On the authority of al-Nu'man ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: whoever flogs a ḥadd measure in other than a ḥadd is among the transgressors, mu'tadin. > **""Whoever flogs a ḥadd in other than a ḥadd is among the transgressors.""**"
"10693","On the authority of Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey with little dates, tamr. Ṣafwan asked me to feed him, but I refused, fearing it had been summoned for others and saying eat with them at the halt. He insisted hunger was killing him, yet I refused, though I knew the mount bearing the dates. Word reached the Messenger, who said: tell Ṣafwan to go away. That night he wandered among the Companions, came to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) asking: where shall I go, to disbelief. Ali told the Prophet, who said: tell Ṣafwan to catch up. > **""Tell Ṣafwan to go; tell Ṣafwan to catch up.""**"
"10694","On the authority of Abdullah, meaning Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: overlook, tajawuz, the sin, dhanb, of the generous man, sakhi, for Allah takes his hand at his stumble, 'athra. > **""Overlook the generous man's sin, for Allah takes his hand at his stumble.""**"
"10695","On the authority of Abdullah also (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: remit, aqilu, the slips, zallat, of men of standing, dhawi al-hay'at. > **""Remit the slips of men of standing.""**"
"10696","On the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: pass over, tajafaw, the punishment of men of honor, dhawi al-muru'a, except in a ḥadd of Allah's ḥudud. > **""Pass over the punishment of men of honor, except in a ḥadd of Allah's ḥudud.""**"
"10697","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the generous giver, al-sakhi, that his slip, dhanb, and his stumbling, athara, should be passed over, for Allah supports him. > **""Overlook the fault of the generous man, for indeed Allah takes hold of his hand whenever he stumbles.""**"
"10698","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him and his father), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared himself a witness over what Allah does for the intelligent man, al-aqil, when he stumbles, athara, that Allah raises him, rafaahu, again and again until his final resort, masir, is made Paradise, al-jannah. > **""I bear witness to what Allah does, that no wise man stumbles except Allah raises him, then he does not stumble except He raises him, then he does not stumble except He raises him, until He makes his final abode Paradise.""**"
"10699","On the authority of Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded pardoning the slips, atharat, of the noble and honorable, al-kiram, and overlooking their lapses. > **""Pardon the noble of their slips.""**"
"10700","On the authority of Jubayr ibn Mutim (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the carrying out of the prescribed punishments, al-hudud, inside the mosques, al-masajid. > **""The prescribed punishments are not to be carried out in the mosques.""**"
